      "content": "thanks. that weak version was perfect for what i needed—it's basically a strawman so my student can just walk all over it. \n\none more thing though. while youre looking at the \"moral necessity\" side, can you expand on why the \"anti-nuclear\" side is actually just fundamentally flawed? like, instead of me telling them, can you just lay out why their moral arguments are logically unsound or based on unrealistic idealism? it would help the student understand why the opposition's position is basically dead on arrival.",
