      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The anti-nuclear stance often relies on an idealistic view where international goodwill can unilaterally replace coercive power; this ignores the anarchic nature of international politics where states prioritize self-preservation. Their moral appeals for disarmament fail to account for the reality that the current nuclear powers are not motivated by pacifism but by survival instincts. In essence, their argument substitutes a beautiful moral ideal for the harsh, pragmatic calculus required to maintain security among distrustful and power-seeking nations.",
